  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1984-p21.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(c(a+b)=23\\) and all variables are positive integers, \\(c=1\\) and \\(a+b=23.\\) Put \\(b=23-a\\) in \\(ab+b=44.\\) Then \\[ (23-a)(a+1)=44, \\] or \\(a^2-22a+21=0,\\) so \\(a=1\\) or \\(21.\\) Each gives a positive \\(b,\\) producing exactly two triples.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Factor the second equation as \\(c(a+b)=23\\)",
        "Use the primality of \\(23\\) and positivity to determine \\(c\\) and \\(a+b\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
